# TypeScript / Next.js Quality Rules

## Type discipline
- No `any` unless explicitly justified.
- Use zod (or equivalent) for runtime validation at API boundaries.

## Next.js patterns
- Server-only secrets: only read env vars on server.
- Never expose secret keys to the client bundle.
- Prefer `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for truly public values.

## Logging
- No logging of request bodies that may include tokens/PII.
- Redact headers like Authorization.

## Output determinism (avoid false confidence)
- Do not make conclusions from truncated command output.
- If output must be limited, say what was omitted and why.
- Prefer complete runs + summarise, rather than early truncation.

## PR hygiene
- Small diffs, clear names, no drive-by refactors unless asked.